<article class="env-lemma" id="0B4X">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0B4X">Lemma <span data-tag="0B4X">54.9.2</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0B4W" data-tag="0B4W">54.9.1</a>. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. Then </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$H^ p(X, \mathcal{F}) = 0$ for $p \not\in \{ 0, 1\} $, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$H^1(X, \mathcal{F}) = 0$ if $\mathcal{F}$ is globally generated. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Part (1) follows from Cohomology of Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/02V7" data-tag="02V7">30.20.9</a>. If $\mathcal{F}$ is globally generated, then there is a surjection $\bigoplus _{i \in I} \mathcal{O}_ X \to \mathcal{F}$. By part (1) and the long exact sequence of cohomology this induces a surjection on $H^1$. Since $H^1(X, \mathcal{O}_ X) = 0$ as $S$ has a rational singularity, and since $H^1(X, -)$ commutes with direct sums (Cohomology, Lemma <a href="/tag/01FF" data-tag="01FF">20.19.1</a>) we conclude. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>